{"id": "make-it-james-ux-upgrade-countercase", "skill": "make-it-james-ux", "status": "response_received", "response": "Optimistic-delete-with-undo is wrong here because the undo would be a lie: once the account is permanently and irrecoverably deleted, there's nothing left to restore. That's not friction reduction, it's a false affordance.\n\nKeep a real blocking confirmation for this action — it's destructive and irreversible, which is exactly the case the \"no confirmation\" rule excludes. Standard pattern: explicit confirm step (e.g., type account name/email, or a confirm dialog stating \"This cannot be undone\"), then delete immediately with no toast implying reversibility. If you want to soften it without lying, offer a real grace period (e.g., 24–48h soft-delete before permanent purge) — but only if that's actually implemented server-side, not simulated in the UI.", "elapsed_seconds": 6.565687833, "provider_metadata": {"host_version": "2.1.220 (Claude Code)", "help_hash": "fcd5b45507c7c602d54d85a300eab288a8a3c6770c6def696ca19a3100725de4", "model_usage": {"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001": {"inputTokens": 572, "outputTokens": 13, "cacheReadInputTokens": 0, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 0, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 0.000637, "contextWindow": 200000, "maxOutputTokens": 32000, "canonicalModel": "claude-haiku-4-5", "provider": "firstParty"}, "claude-sonnet-5": {"inputTokens": 2, "outputTokens": 250, "cacheReadInputTokens": 0, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 2353, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 0.017874, "contextWindow": 1000000, "maxOutputTokens": 64000, "canonicalModel": "claude-sonnet-5", "provider": "firstParty"}}, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2353, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 250, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 2353, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "not_available", "iterations"